WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.128
Raj: Our growth forecast assumes current retention. Net storage grows two hundred gigabytes monthly.

2
00:00:07.128 --> 00:00:13.440
Hannah: Is that measured growth or projection? Include how many months you sampled.

3
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.800
Raj: Measured across the last six months. Campaign demand is a separate assumption.

4
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:26.664
Priya: Just to confirm, net after retention, right? Don't subtract those deletions twice.

5
00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:33.216
Lukas: Exactly. A campaign could change the slope. Show a high-growth case as well.

6
00:00:33.216 --> 00:00:40.104
Anika: Our working hypothesis allows a larger burst. Maybe three times normal campaign writes.

7
00:00:40.104 --> 00:00:47.784
Hannah: That's not three times monthly storage automatically. Burst duration matters for that estimate.

8
00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:54.816
Priya: Okay, what's the ETA for campaign inputs? One action item is verified duration.

9
00:00:54.816 --> 00:01:01.008
Lukas: I'll ask business owners this afternoon. We shouldn't invent an exact demand curve.

10
00:01:01.008 --> 00:01:08.160
Anika: So, I've got bandwidth for scenarios. First compare today's actual performance baseline.

